is is fine for those  at the top  they have the wealth to weather a  year-long crisis 99  of americans do not what is it going to  take to get the people of this country  to realize that not only can we not  handle crises  our predatory capitalist system actively  causes the crisis  capitalism cannot and will not solve the  problems it creates  we have a homelessness crisis at the  same time as an excess of housing  why housing the homeless isn't  profitable we maintain low-level wars  for decades at tremendous cost of human  life  why because war is profitable the  military-industrial complex is one of  our biggest industries  it's why we ignore humanitarian crises  like the war in yemen  the united states arms the people  responsible for the massacre  what happens when the next crisis is  worse how many americans have to die  before we realize that capitalism is  destroying us  we already have another ticking time  bomb on the horizon each successive  generation is less well-off than the  previous one  older generations those who experience  the final years of comfort for the  average american worker are dying off  younger people don't have the buying  power their parents and grandparents did  we're having fewer children mostly  because we can't afford to raise  children  fewer children means fewer people to  grow up and buy things  what happens when a country built on  consumerism runs out of people to buy  those products  consumption falls off a cliff gdp  plummets businesses flee to other  countries  poverty skyrockets and the american  empire implodes  it's not some innate characteristic of  the us that makes us incapable of  handling crises  any country with a system as  hyper-capitalist as ours would suffer  similarly poor performance  if you look around the world there are  plenty of mostly capitalist countries  that handle the pandemic much better  than the us  what's the difference they have their  guard rails intact  social safety nets robust unemployment  assistance universal healthcare  their citizens are more secure their  business is less predatory  they haven't deregulated and privatized  their countries into oblivion  in america we've removed those  guardrails and stepped on the gas  after all the biggest profits are right  at the edge of the cliff  capitalism is why we can't handle crises  if you're familiar with my channel you  know that my perspective is very  us-centric  it's what i know best if you'd like to  get a more global perspective on this  topic  make sure to check out ugopnik's video  next it's a fantastic companion piece to  this video  if you enjoyed this episode consider  dropping a like if you hated it a thumbs  down  you can check out my previous episodes  by clicking the links on your screen  thanks for watching and i'll see you  next week
 

